<title>PARAGUAY: Paraguay ministers to discuss telecom company sale.</title>
<headline>Paraguay ministers to discuss telecom company sale.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paraguayan ministers on Monday were scheduled to discuss legislation allowing the sale of 70 percent of Antelco, the state-owned telecommunications company, a government official said.</p>
<p>The initial plan is for the state to maintain a 20 percent stake, with the remaining 10 percent distributed to Antelco workers, the official, who asked not to be named, told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said the government hoped to finish drafting the bill within a week to send to it Congress.</p>
<p>-- Jose Maria Amarilla, Asuncion Newsroom +59521 44-4527</p>
</text>
